(vector
 (map
  (:adr/id "adr-2609111100-hokusai-is-two-models-and-the-video-one-cannot-say-no")
  (:adr/title "hokusai is two models under one name, and the video one cannot follow a negative instruction")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2609102000-hokusai-is-a-name-the-fleet-owns"
                        "adr-2609111000-shinshi-club-runs-on-four-planes-and-three-were-silent"
                        "adr-2609092400-murakumo-public-examples-hanzo-confidential-admission"))
  (:adr/body "
## The instruction

Owner, 2026-09-11: 「今の murakumo.cloud の hokusai モデルを作って, シーンも生成して」,
then 「両方」 (image and video), then 「生成したら公開も合わせて進めて」.

## What hokusai was, measured before touching anything

| name | what it is | state at 01:10Z |
|---|---|---|
| `awai-network/hokusai` (ADR-2609102000, 09-10) | image name → `waiREALMIX_v11` on gad ComfyUI `:8188`, `POST /v1/images/generations` | live: 200, 512×512 PNG, 9.2 s. **`GET /infer/models/awai-network/hokusai` → `no such model`** — it existed only as a rewrite in the gateway's JS entry |
| `hokusai` (KV entry, verified 09-04) | video: MiniMax H3 / 10Eros-Max TURBO-hybrid beta4 int8 on gad ComfyUI-h3 `:8191` | live, 48 GB VRAM |
| `manifest/awai-model-seed.edn :hokusai` (Codex seed, 09-08) | video, `:trained-artifact nil`, six eval prompts | seed only |

Two live models share the name; the seed describes a third state (trained) that
does not exist. This ADR does not merge them — it makes each one legible.

## Image: catalog entry + shinshi scenes (done, public)

- `PUT /infer/models/awai-network/hokusai` with kind, checkpoint, endpoint,
  sizes, `free: true`, the smoke measurement, and a note saying it is NOT the
  video `hokusai`. `status-evidence` reads `fresh`. Written with the fleet's
  service bearer read from a node's `~/.murakumo/edge/join.env` — the value
  kagi does not hold (secrets map, still true today).
- `scripts/shinshi-cast-bots/generate.cljs image` now names the model
  (`SHINSHI_IMAGE_MODEL`, default `awai-network/hokusai`) and prints it in
  its receipt (root #3092). 12/12 cast members received one scene; each is
  served at `shinshi.club/b/<sha256>` with the served bytes hashing to the
  receipt, and registered in D1 `scene` (botan-amano-noir: 0 → 1).

## Video: six eval scenes on the serving checkpoint (done, public)

Graph: gad's smoke-verified `t2v_api.json`, beta4 int8 unet, 768×512,
144 frames requested (158 delivered = 6.58 s @ 24 fps; the rubrics are written
for 6 s), 8 steps (the TURBO setting `eros-smoke.json` used). Sequential, one
job at a time, GPU 100% for the run.

    clip   elapsed   rubric   what it missed
    h-e01  1240 s    2/5      a hand; printed text on the cup
    h-e02  1160 s    4/5      a character already written on the paper
    h-e03  1100 s    2/5      a person appears and speaks; a road, not a garden
    h-e04  1180 s    1/5      >3 lanterns; the PROMPT printed on the lanterns; audio
    h-e05  1140 s    2/5      ripples before 4 s and many; audio (not silent)
    h-e06  1100 s    2/4      background light never changes; audio

13 of 29 rubric items. The scores are one operator's read of frames at
0.5 / 3.0 / 5.8 s plus `volumedetect`; they are not a model judge, and every
clip is public with its score in the title so anyone can disagree against
the bytes. Full receipts: `manifest/awai-model-seed.edn` `:hokusai :eval-runs`.

**The finding that matters is the pattern, not the average.** Every clip
that lost a point lost it on a NEGATIVE instruction — 無人 / 文字なし /
音楽なし / 無音 / 一つだけ — and in three of six the model rendered the
prompt's own words as text inside the picture (紙, 提灯が三つ, 湯). The
positive content (steam, brush, rain, lanterns, leaf, cup) is there in all
six. Whatever training the seed imagines, it has to teach 'not', and the eval
set already measures exactly that.

## Publication: the examples plane carries video without a Worker change

murakumo.cloud's public-examples plane (ADR-2609092400) serves an approved
row's `mime_type` from R2 as-is, so `video/mp4` rows are served with the
same no-store / nosniff / sandbox headers as PNG. The operator half the
Worker deliberately lacks is now `cloud-murakumo/scripts/publish-artifact.cljk`
(#185; landed as `.cljs`, renamed by the cljk wave minutes later): sha256 →
R2 put under `preview-artifacts/v1/<uuid>` → D1 `pending` → the doc's exact
UPDATE bound to `status='pending'` → read-back through the public URL that
must hash to the stored digest before it says `published`. Six rows, six
sha256 matches, consent version `operator-eval-v1` (no third-party input
existed to consent).

Not done, on purpose:
- inline `<video>` on the homepage card (the site script inlines `image`
  only; other kinds get title + link). `cloud-murakumo-site` renamed to
  `.cljk` the same hour; whether `kbb -M:site` still renders it is a
  separate measurement, so the data-plane publish shipped without it.
- byte-range serving. The Worker streams the object whole; Safari may
  refuse progressive mp4 without `Range`. Chrome/Firefox play it.
- training. `:trained-artifact` stays nil; this run is the untrained baseline
  the seed lacked.

## Seen while doing this, not fixed here

- The `.cljk` rename wave (root `780284efa66`, 987 files at 12:02 JST) renamed
  `scripts/nbb_compat.cljs` too. nbb resolves a required namespace to
  `.cljs`/`.cljc` only, so **the 60 root scripts that `(require
  '[scripts.nbb-compat])` now fail at load** — `root-worktree`, `west-pin-put`
  among them (measured 03:15Z; `west-pin-put` had worked at 02:47Z, before
  the rename). This ADR's worktree was cut by hand with `git worktree add`
  + cone sparse-checkout for that reason.
- `network-awai/hokusai` also exists in the catalog (org spelled the other
  way round). Left alone.
")))
